    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0048" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg36"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.01/4–1846: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Certain Diplomatic and Consular
                        Officers</hi><anchor n="34" xml:id="d38-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-18T13:00:00-05:00">April 18, 1946—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Vietnam Republic’s President Ho Chi-minh requested US, UK and other recognitions
                    approximating French recognition as free state within French Union. UK
                    informally replied unable recognize because negotiations re Vietnam actual
                    status continuing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d38-f1" n="34" type="source" xml:id="d38-f1-content">
                <p>At Bangkok, Batavia, Chungking, London, Manila, Paris, and The Hague.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
